!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/link/valid/an-ordinary-schema-names-a-value-through-cores-ref-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/link-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §2.2.3, [TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2"
  description: """
    An ordinary schema imports no meta-kernel, so the kernel's `ref` is not in its namespace; core declares a
    sibling under the same name, and a schema importing core types a field `ref<order>` through it. `order` is
    a type of the schema's own namespace, which is where a reference's `T` resolves.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  valid: {
    binds: [order pick ref kind]
  }
}
